Using Lemma \ref{DCFLC} we show that if a Delone configuration of finite local complexity has a line $\R^d$-polynomial annihilator, then it is periodic.
In the proofs of the following results for a non-zero vector $\bv \in \R^d$, by a $\bv$-fiber of an $\R^d$-configuration $c \in \A^{\R^d}$ we mean an $\R$-configuration $e^{(\bu)} \in \A^{\R}$ for some $\bu \in \R^d$ defined such that 
$$
e^{(\bu)}_r = c_{\bu + r \bv}
$$
for all $r \in \R$.


\begin{lemma} \label{line polynomial annihilator implies periodicity}
  Let $c \in \A^{\R^d}$ be a Delone configuration of finite local complexity and assume that it is annihilated by a line $\R^d$-polynomial $f$ in direction $\bv$. 
  Then $c$ is periodic in direction $\bv$.
\end{lemma}

