\begin{proof}
    % Sampleable area
    %Before placing our robots we wish to find a subset of the area so as to create a more comfortable configuration space. There is no assumption made on the type of two-dimensional space given, so we limit the possible sampled area to a bounded circle with the largest radius ($\B$) such that $\X'^N_f=\max\{\}$\roy{I don't know how to write this :(}. This circle is of area $S_\B = \pi R_\B^2$.
