  \caption{The Kolumbo dataset chunked into nine parts, each rendered separately using a volume texture for each chunk with the \textit{TBRayMarcher} plugin. The scene is displayed in our ARENA2 visualization dome.}
  \label{fig:Kolumbo_TBRM_Dome1}
\end{figure}

This approach allows for beautiful rendering with great performance on a single machine, at least on the RTX 3500 Ada GPU, see section \ref{sec:results}.
Here, VRAM seems to be the biggest limiting factor.

\begin{figure}[H]
  \centering
  %\fbox{\rule[-.5cm]{4cm}{4cm} \rule[-.5cm]{4cm}{0cm}
  \includegraphics[width=1.0\textwidth]{media/Kolumbo_TBRM_ChunkBorders.jpg}
