The reduced speed primarily comes from the dominance of the time-consuming reconstruction process as the number of mismatches between ISS and RTL simulations increases. Besides, the original PCAP mechanism of Xilinx is able to encrypt the bitstream for security \cite{amdILA}. To obtain the least latency between PS and PL, our PCAP bridge runs in non-secure mode with a maximum bandwidth of approximately 140 MB/s, while the overall data transmission rate is limited by the PS AXI interconnect. In addition, the PL frames read back via PCAP contain a considerable amount of data for padding, therefore reducing the actual throughput.
