\subsubsection{ResNet50 as Feature Encoder to Prototypes (R50-E2P)}
\label{sec:our_method}
%
Building on the recent strategy that effectively leverages ViT \cite{cozzolino_raising_2024}, this study explores whether similar improvements in generalization and robustness to unseen generators and data processing can be achieved using R50-ND with frozen ImageNet-pretrained weights as a feature encoder.

{Indeed, \cite{cozzolino_raising_2024} demonstrates that ViT-based forensic detectors, pre-trained on large datasets of non-synthetic media, inherently encode fundamental properties of real images, and these properties not only help distinguish real from fake images but also enable superior generalization to unseen generative pipelines compared to fully retrained detectors like R50-ND.}
However, since R50-ND was also pre-trained on ImageNet \cite{imagenet15russakovsky} (another large dataset of real images) we hypothesize that its weaker generalization ability is primarily due to catastrophic forgetting \cite{kirkpatrick2017overcoming}.
%\Giulia{Mimicking the recent effective strategy exploiting ViT in \cite{cozzolino_raising_2024}, in this study we investigate whether improvements in terms of generalization and robustness to unseen generators and data processing can be achieved also by utilizing R50-ND with frozen ImageNet-pretrained weights as a feature encoder.
%Indeed, we already mentioned that Cozzolino et al. in \cite{cozzolino_raising_2024} demonstrated that ViT-based forensic detectors, pre-trained on large datasets of non-synthetic media, inherently encode fundamental properties of real media also useful to distinguish real from fake images, and this approach outperforms fully retrained detectors, such as R50-ND, in terms of generalization to unseen generative pipelines.
%But since also R50-ND was pre-trained on ImageNet \cite{imagenet15russakovsky} (another large dataset of real images), we believe its lower generalization ability is likely due to \textit{catastrophic forgetting}~\cite{kirkpatrick2017overcoming}.} %a phenomenon that arises when a model is retrained on a limited set of training samples.} 
%\Giulia{forse si può dire meglio ma intanto l'ho rivista così...}



Specifically, features extracted by R50-ND will be classified by a shallow, trainable classification head consisting of a single fully connected layer. This layer reduces the feature dimensionality from 2048 to 128 while implementing learned prototypes \cite{lee2020multi,ruff2018deep}. Learned prototypes are commonly used in deep learning classification tasks to detect out-of-distribution samples by modeling an isotropic Gaussian class-conditional distribution representative of the input data.

%By adopting this approach, we simultaneously learn the feature space mapping induced by the fully connected layer and the parameters that define the isotropic distributions of real and fake images through learned prototypes.

If \(\mathbf{f}\) represents the features extracted by the fully connected layer of R50-ND with frozen weights, the corresponding learned prototypes are computed as follows:
\begin{equation}  
s(\mathbf{f}) = \left[ \operatorname{sgn} \left( \sum_{k=1}^{D} (f_k - c_k) \right) \cdot \left( \frac{\|\mathbf{f} - \mathbf{c}\|_2}{2\sigma_k^2} \right) + D \ln \sigma_k \right]  
\label{eq:proto_new}  
\nonumber
\end{equation}  
where, \(D\) denotes the input feature dimension, while \(\mathbf{c} = [c_1, \dots, c_D] \in \mathbb{R}^{D}\) represents a set of centroids characterizing an isotropic Gaussian class-conditional distribution with standard deviations \(\boldsymbol{\sigma} = [\sigma_1, \dots, \sigma_D] \in \mathbb{R}^{D}\).
Both \(\mathbf{c}\) and \(\boldsymbol{\sigma}\) are learned during training and are constrained by \(\log \sigma_k > 0, \forall k\), ensuring that the distance function satisfies the triangle inequality, an essential property for using learned prototypes as a valid metric \cite{lee2020multi}. Finally, we incorporated the term \(\operatorname{sgn} \left( \sum_{k=1}^{D} (f_k - c_k) \right)\) to enhance performance in binary classification tasks \footnote{Full training and testing code {is available at \url{https://github.com/MMLab-unitn/TrueFake-IJCNN25}}}.

%{In Sect.~\ref{sec:experimental_results} we will refer to this method with the name ResNet50-Encoder2Prototypes (R50-E2P).}


