\subsection{Submesh interface}
A recent addition to MFEM is its submesh interface, which allows applications to define a mesh that represents a subset of a parent mesh.
Subsets can be formed from volume elements or boundary elements, creating domain or surface meshes, respectively.
A submesh is a fully functional MFEM mesh, and so all of MFEM's existing machinery can be used on one or multiple submeshes.
Furthermore, MFEM provides the ability to transfer grid functions between a parent mesh and its submeshes or between submeshes that share the same parent Mesh.
Let $S_P^A$ denote the operator that extracts a submesh grid function $u_A$ from the parent grid function $u_p$,  such that $u_A = S_P^A u_p$. We can use this operator to also extend  submesh grid functions to the full mesh and to exchange data between submeshes. See~\Cref{fig_submesh} for an illustration.
